==========
psion/opl #1928, from jezar, 1200 chars, May 4 13:18 95
----------
Changing the text of a DTEXT

Some people have been asking how to change the text of a DTEXT 
dynamically when running under my APPMAN.OPL

Well, you can use the following routine to do this. Note that, ideally, 
you might also like to do a gINFO "Press Tab to change this item" if 
someone presses anything other than Tab, or another key the dialog cannot 
handle while the cursor is on the relevant DTEXT item.

Here is the procedure:

PROC dTXTSET%:(itm%,text$) REM Set the text
        
        LOCAL ret%
        
        REM This LOCAL data is ALL used!
        REM SE_TEXTWIN struct:
        LOCAL flags%,stat%,text%,len%
        
        LOCAL txt$(255)
        
        REM Check that the dialog box exists
        IF PEEKW($36)=0
                RAISE -85
        ENDIF
        
        txt$=text$
        text%=ADDR(txt$)+1
        len%=LEN(txt$)
        flags%=8      REM (SE_TEXTWIN_TEXT)
        CALL($0dd6,0,0,0)  REM Enable ws leaves
        REM Tell the dialog box to set item
        ret%=ENTERSEND0(PEEKW($36),10,#itm%,flags%)
        CALL($0dd6,0,0,1)  REM Disable ws leaves
        IF ret%
                RAISE ret%
        ENDIF
ENDP



